<title>FRANCE: CYCLING-MIDI LIBRE THIRD STAGE PLACINGS.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-MIDI LIBRE THIRD STAGE PLACINGS.</headline>
<dateline>ALES, France 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading placings in the</p>
<p>182-kms third stage of the Midi Libre cycling race from St Chely</p>
<p>d'Apcher to Ales on Thursday:</p>
<p>Stage placings:</p>
<p>1. Laurent Brochard (France) Festina    4 hours 16 minutes and</p>
<p>seven seconds</p>
<p>2. Orlando Gomes-Rodrigues (Spain) Banesto</p>
<p>3. Bo Hamburger (Denmark) TVM</p>
<p>4. Jean-Cyril Robin (France) US Postal Service same time</p>
<p>5. Angel Casero-Moreno (Spain) Banesto	   8 secs behind</p>
<p>6. Thierry Gouvenou (France) Bigmat Auber 93   6:23</p>
<p>7. Adriano Baffi (Italy) US Postal Service     6:31</p>
<p>8. Rolf Aladag (Germany) Telekom   </p>
<p>9. Andrei Teteriuk (Kazakhstan) Lotto	    </p>
<p>10. Frederic Moncassin (France) GAN		 all same time</p>
<p>Leading overall standings:</p>
<p> 1. Alberto Elli (Italy) Casino     15 hours 13 minutes</p>
<p>and nine seconds</p>
<p> 2. Laurent Dufaux (Switzerland) Festina	    8:14</p>
<p> 3. Bart Voskamp (Netherlands) TVM		    8:22</p>
<p> 4. Georg Totschnig (Germany) Telekom		 8:23</p>
<p> 5. Arturas Kasputis (Lithuania) Casino	     8:26</p>
<p> 6. David Plaza (France) Cofidis			8:26</p>
<p> 7. Bo Hamburger (Denmark) TVM			 11:51</p>
<p> 8. Angel Casero-Moreno (Spain) Banesto	    12:23</p>
<p> 9. Laurent Desbiens (France) Cofidis		18:26</p>
<p>10. Luca Gelfi (Italy) Brescialat		    18:44</p>
</text>
